Subject: [PATCH 287/333] [ae-patch] Tell the user when queued notes wait for
 sign-in, and fix the 0282 notes

Fix-check fixes to the previous patch (2026-11-01).

Notes carried because the current identity could not be verified were held
with no toast (only console.info said carried=N), and the restore awaited
resolveIdentity() with no cap, so a /v1/me call that hung right after a
deploy held the notes silently for the page's life; retyping them meant a
later reload sent both. The identity wait is now capped at 10 s, after
which the identity counts as unverifiable, and any carried notes get one
toast saying they wait until sign-in is confirmed, to reload rather than
retype. New tests cover a hanging probe hitting the cap, a failed probe
with stored owned notes, and a toast that counts only carried notes.
